<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy – StillOn" %>

<div class="sms-page">
  <div class="sms-shell">

    <div class="sms-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul class="sms-list">
        <li><strong>Organizers:</strong> first name, phone number. That's it — no email, no password.</li>
        <li><strong>Guests:</strong> name and, if you choose to provide it, your phone number for day-of reminders. Both are voluntary beyond your name.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage:</strong> which pages of the signup and RSVP flows were opened and whether an RSVP was sent, along with browser type, device type and the referring site. We don't record IP addresses or location.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul class="sms-list">
        <li>Your phone number is used only to send you SMS messages directly related to hangouts you're involved in — verification codes, RSVP reminders, and day-of reminders.</li>
        <li>Usage data is used only to see where people get stuck in signup and RSVPs, so we can make them easier. It stays in our own database.</li>
        <li>We don't use your data for advertising. We don't sell it. We don't share it with third parties except Twilio, our SMS provider, solely to deliver messages.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>If you RSVP with a phone number, we save it in a cookie on your device. This is purely functional — it lets us pre-fill your RSVP form the next time you visit an invite link, so you don't have to type your number again. The cookie expires after one year.</p>
      <p>We also set two first-party analytics cookies, <code>ahoy_visit</code> (expires after 4 hours) and <code>ahoy_visitor</code> (expires after 2 years). They hold random IDs that let us count unique visitors through signup and RSVPs. They aren't shared with anyone or used for advertising.</p>
      <p>You can clear these at any time by clearing your browser cookies. The phone cookie is also removed automatically if you RSVP and leave the phone field blank.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>SMS opt-out</h2>
      <p>Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message to unsubscribe. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for support. Message and data rates may apply. For full details on our SMS program, see the <%= link_to "SMS Program page", sms_info_path %>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>Guest RSVP data (name, phone) is tied to a specific event occurrence and is not used after the event passes. If you'd like your data removed, email us and we'll take care of it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="sms-section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Reach us at <strong>hello@stillon.app</strong>.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>
